            <notesStmt>  
                
                <note type="project" target="#dat1">Whitman must have written this manuscript fragment in 1890, sometime between 27 April (the date of the postmark on the reverse) and 10 May (the date written on a <ref target="loc.00239">late draft</ref> of the same poem).</note>                
                <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.0383" cert="high">The lines on this manuscript contributed to the poem "On, On the Same, Ye Jocund Twain!" which was first published in <hi rend="italic">Good-Bye My Fancy</hi> (1891). The poem also appeared shortly thereafter in the 9 June 1891 issue of <hi rend="italic">Once a Week</hi>.</note>
